# Configuration required before this workflow will run
#
# The sanitised export in this directory contains no working configuration by
# design. Every value below is either a placeholder literal inside
# n8n-workflow.sanitized.json that must be substituted, or a credential that
# must be created in the n8n instance.
#
# Copy to .env for your own record keeping if useful. n8n does not read this
# file: the workflow embeds literals rather than $env references, so that a
# reader can see the shape of every identifier without running anything.
# Substituting them is a deliberate manual step, not a deployment convenience.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Literal placeholders inside the workflow JSON
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Find each with:  grep -n '<<' n8n-workflow.sanitized.json
#                  grep -n 'example.invalid\|C0000\|0000000000' n8n-workflow.sanitized.json

# Path segment of the webhook that receives Slack modal submissions.
# Appears in: ITK 01 Receive request submission -> parameters.path
# Use a long random segment. This endpoint is unauthenticated at the transport
# layer and its obscurity is not a security control; see note 4 below.
INTAKE_WEBHOOK_PATH=<<INTAKE_WEBHOOK_PATH>>

# Numeric space id of the Confluence space that receives published pages.
# Appears in: PUB 01 Create documentation page -> jsonBody
DOCS_SPACE_ID=<<DOCS_SPACE_ID>>

# Base URL of the documentation platform, currently https://example.invalid/wiki
# Appears in: DFT 01 Load knowledge pack, PUB 01 Create documentation page
# Real shape: https://your-site.atlassian.net/wiki
DOCS_BASE_URL=https://example.invalid/wiki

# Registry database. Currently the all-zero UUID.
# Appears in: REG 01 Create request record -> databaseId
REGISTRY_DATABASE_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Slack channel ids. Currently shape-preserving placeholders.
# Appears in: ORC 04 Resolve routing rule -> ROUTING table (reviewerChannel)
SLACK_CHANNEL_INTAKE=C00000000000
SLACK_CHANNEL_FINANCE_REVIEW=C00000000001
SLACK_CHANNEL_COMPLIANCE_REVIEW=C00000000002
SLACK_CHANNEL_BACKEND_REVIEW=C00000000003

# Confluence parent page ids, one per request type.
# Appears in: ORC 04 Resolve routing rule -> ROUTING table (parentPageId)
PARENT_PAGE_FEE=0000000001
PARENT_PAGE_RAIL=0000000002
PARENT_PAGE_RISK=0000000003
PARENT_PAGE_RPT=0000000004
PARENT_PAGE_MEX=0000000005
PARENT_PAGE_INT=0000000006

# Knowledge pack and template identifiers, one per request type.
# Appears in: ORC 04 Resolve routing rule -> ROUTING table (template)
# Currently slugs such as brd-fee-change. Replace with real page ids or keep
# slugs if the documentation platform resolves them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Credentials to create in n8n
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The export references four credentials by placeholder id and generic name.
# On import n8n will show them as unresolved. Create each one, then reassign it
# on the nodes listed. Do not paste secrets into node parameters.
#
#   Slack account            -> Slack API, bot token
#                               Scopes: chat:write, chat:write.public, users:read
#                               Used by: ORC 09, REV 01, PUB 02, PUB 03, PUB 04
#
#   Registry account         -> Notion API, internal integration token
#                               The integration must be shared with the registry
#                               database. Grant insert and update, not delete.
#                               Used by: REG 01, REG 03, REG 04, REG 05, REG 06, REG 07
#
#   Documentation platform   -> Header Auth
#                               Header: Authorization
#                               Value:  Basic <base64 of email:api-token>
#                               Used by: DFT 01, PUB 01
#
#   LLM provider             -> Header Auth
#                               Header: x-api-key
#                               Used by: DFT 02
#
# Scope each credential to the minimum the pipeline needs. The drafting agent
# holds none of these; it receives text and returns text, and every write is
# performed by n8n.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Registry schema expected by the workflow
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Notion database must have these properties with these exact names and
# types, or the REG nodes will fail on property mapping.
#
#   Name                  title
#   Status                select   Submitted | Classified | Drafted | In review |
#                                  Published | Rejected | Needs input
#   Type                  select   FEE | RAIL | RISK | RPT | MEX | INT
#   Requesting team       rich_text
#   Reviewer role         select   Finance Approver | Compliance Reviewer |
#                                  Backend Reviewer
#   Review SLA hours      number
#   Submitted at          date
#   Review requested at   date
#   Decided at            date
#   Open gaps             number
#   Decision reason       rich_text
#   Published page        url
#   Approved by role      select

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Known gaps in this reference export
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stated rather than left to be discovered.
#
#   Webhook authentication. ITK 01 verifies nothing. A real deployment must
#   validate the Slack request signature before ORC 01 runs. This is omitted
#   here because the verification node is instance-specific, not because it is
#   optional.
#
#   Sequence generation. REG 02 derives the request number from workflow static
#   data, which is not safe against concurrent executions and will collide under
#   load. Replace with a registry count query or a dedicated counter.
#
#   Resume URL exposure. REV 01 posts approve, reject and needs-input links into
#   a Slack channel. Anyone in that channel can act on them, and the resulting
#   decision is attributed to the reviewer role rather than to an individual.
#   This is adequate for a role-scoped private channel and inadequate for
#   anything requiring individual attribution or non-repudiation.
#
#   No error workflow. Failures surface in the n8n execution log only. Nothing
#   notifies the requester that their request stopped moving.
#
#   No SLA enforcement. Review SLA hours is recorded and never acted on. There
#   is deliberately no timeout that auto-approves; see not-automated.md.
